        "majority_choice": 0,
        "candidates": [
          {
            "index": 0,
            "parsed_answer": "16",
            "ending": "and all songs except one lasted 5 minutes.\n\n- Total time of the concert: 1 hour 20 minutes = 90 minutes.\n- Intermission: 10 minutes.\n- Time spent singing: 90 - 10 = 80 minutes.\n- Number of songs: 80 / 5 = 16 songs.\n\n#### <numeric answer> 16"
          },
          {
            "index": 1,
            "parsed_answer": "14",
            "ending": "e songs were **5 minutes** except for one song that lasted **10 minutes**.\n   - So, the total time for all songs is:\n     $$\n     70 = 6 \\times 10 + 10 = 70\n     $$\n   - Number of songs = $70 \\div 5 = 14$\n\n### Final Answer:\n$$\n\\boxed{14}\n$$"
          },
          {
            "index": 2,
            "parsed_answer": "13",
            "ending": " songs is $ 5(x - 1) $ minutes.\n- The time for the **10-minute song** is 10 minutes.\n\nSo the total time is:\n\n$$\n5(x - 1) + 10 = 70\n$$\n\nSolving:\n\n$$\n5x - 5 + 10 = 70 \\\\\n5x + 5 = 70 \\\\\n5x = 65 \\\\\nx = 13\n$$\n\n### Final Answer:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{13}\n$$"
          },
          {
            "index": 3,
            "parsed_answer": "12",
            "ending": "mber of songs**:  \n   The songs lasted 5 minutes except for one song that lasted 10 minutes. So, the total time is:  \n   $60 = 5 \\times 12 + 10$  \n   $60 = 60 + 10$ \u2705\n\n   Therefore, the number of songs is **12**.\n\n#### Final answer: **12**."
          }
        ]
